    Add the inner-dimension sumcheck to the request reduction
    
    The request reduction gains its inner dimension: the claim is the equality-weighted product of the two operand maps at an inner point, the sumcheck runs one equality weight per inner bit, and the weighted product inner carries the later variables' equality factors. Focused tests compute the claim by hand, prove and verify it, and refuse a pair whose product sum does not match.
    
    This is partial progress: the stack rounds and the affine row claims are the next step.

